{
 "note": "The Goose, beachfront restaurant on the Busselton foreshore by the jetty (South West Architects 2005, rebuilt after the 2021 fire to the same form), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and photos. Three steep white Colorbond gables with charcoal weatherboard gable ends, white barges and triangular apex windows, full-width white-framed glazing below, a long lower roof along the beach side with four small open verandah gables over the deck, flat roofs at the kitchen (south-west) and east end, and timber decks with a white wire balustrade. It has no street: the front here is the south side, towards the lawn, Foreshore Parade and the jetty car park, which is what drivers see. The name is plain lettering, no goose logo. Metres: x left to right as seen from the south (west to east), y back from the south face (towards the beach).",
